A||N||7||kong||engine swap||||
Z||000000||kong||09-09-1999||02:27 PM||||Hello all; Ihave an 87 coupe with 2.5 4cyl. with throttle body inj. I want to swap for 2.8v6 with multi port Iwant to keep my 5 sp. My question is. What mods am I going to have to do to make this as smooth as I can?||||reg||
Z||000001||DJRice||09-10-1999||08:45 AM||||Fuel Pump, motor mounts, dog bone (Torque strut).<P>If you have a donor fiero with a V6, the easiest thing to do is going to be to remove all of the wiring from the engine compartment up to the dash and forward firewall.  Changing the wires is a job that will take several hours, but in the end, you just use swap the ECMs and gauge kits, turn the key and go.<P>If you dont have a Fiero donor car then more power to you......<P>BTW, you need to change the fuel pump, located in gas tank, because the v6 requires more fuel pressure than the 4 cyl.||||reg||
Z||000002||kong||09-10-1999||10:07 AM||||Thanks Rice, Unfortunatly I don't have a donor fiero. this engine is coming out of a 89 celebrity. This is my first swap in a fiero. I'm used to fords and then non-computerized at that. ||||reg||
Z||000003||theogre||09-10-1999||02:12 PM||||Kong, without the Fiero wiring harness you will find this job very dificult. I would contact Kick Hill if you don't have anything in a nearby salvage yard. <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kickhill.com</A> <BR>These guys keep practically everything in stock.<P>If the celebrity has power steering, you could end up changing most of the PTO brackets. Likely the celebrity has to have things moved, like alternator & A/C, to the proper positions for Fiero.<P>You will likely also have to alter or replace the A/C compressor in the Fiero. The 4 cyl in 87 has the serpent belt. The v6 Fiero setup used a Vbelt for the AC. I don't know what the celebrity has, but it's something to watch for.<BR>||||reg||
Z||000004||batboy||09-11-1999||11:49 AM||||Sounds like the guys mentioned most of the swap problems: wiring harness, fuel pump, pulley/belts, motor mounts, etc. But, isn't there a caution about the clutch? I think you have to use the right clutch for the engine. Seems like the other way around causes problems or something. Does anyone else remember this for sure?||||reg||1
Z||000005||PaUL||09-11-1999||01:42 PM||||Hey what you all said is absolutely correct, I should know, my donor car was a 85 celebrity. Strangely it was carbed but had the larger main journals. Must have been made during the transition. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||kong||09-11-1999||05:38 PM||||Thanks to all the people who have responded, this was the first time I have used this forum and I will keep popping in now and then to let you know how it's going. Thanks also to Ogre for the site you gave me, it looks like the easiest way to go. Well, like Arnold aways says "I'll be back".||||reg||1
